abstract:
In this paper, we consider a smooth connected finite-dimensional manifold $M$, an affine connection $
abla$ with holonomy group $H^{
abla}$ and $Δ$ a smooth completely non integrable distribution. We define the $Δ$-horizontal holonomy group $H^{\;
abla}_Δ$ as the subgroup of $H^{
abla}$ obtained by $
abla$-parallel transporting frames only along loops tangent to $Δ$. We first set elementary properties of $H^{\;
abla}_Δ$ and show how to study it using the rolling formalism (\cite{ChitourKokkonen}). In particular, it is shown that $H^{\;
abla}_Δ$ is a Lie group. Moreover, we study an explicit example where $M$ is a free step-two homogeneous Carnot group and $
abla$ is the Levi-Civita connection associated to a Riemannian metric on $M$, and show that in this particular case the connected component of the identity of $H^{\;
abla}_Δ$ is compact and strictly included in $H^{
abla}$.

A real seminormed involutive algebra is a real associative algebra ${\mathcal A}$ endowed with an involutive antiautomorphism $*$ and a submultiplicative seminorm $p$ with $p(a^*) =p(a)$ for $a\in {\mathcal A}$. Then ${\mathop{	t ball}
olimits}({\mathcal A},p) := \{a \in {\mathcal A} \colon p(a) < 1\}$ is an involutive subsemigroup. For the case where ${\mathcal A}$ is unital, our main result asserts that a function $ϕ\colon{\mathop{	t ball}
olimits}({\mathcal A},p) 	o B(V)$, $V$ a Hilbert space, is completely positive (defined suitably) if and only if it is positive definite and analytic for any locally convex topology for which ${\mathop{	t ball}
olimits}({\mathcal A},p)$ is open. If $η_{\mathcal A} \colon {\mathcal A} 	o C^*({\mathcal A},p)$ is the enveloping $C^*$-algebra of $({\mathcal A},p)$ and $e^{C^*({\mathcal A},p)}$ is the $c_0$-direct sum of the symmetric tensor powers $S^n(C^*({\mathcal A},p))$, then the above two properties are equivalent to the existence of a factorization $ϕ= Φ\circ Γ$, where $Φ\colon e^{C^*({\mathcal A},p)} 	o B(V)$ is linear completely positive and $Γ(a) = \sum_{n = 0}^\infty η_{\mathcal A}(a)^{\otimes n}$. We also obtain a suitable generalization to non-unital algebras. An important consequence of this result is a description of the unitary representations of ${m U}({\mathcal A})$ with bounded analytic extensions to ${\mathop{	t ball}
olimits}({\mathcal A},p)$ in terms of representations of the $C^*$-algebra $e^{C^*({\mathcal A},p)}$.
